{"step_index":27,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T05:18:58Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"**GTU Mid-Sem Master Cheat Sheet: Tier 1 & Easy Wins (UPDATED)**\\nThis document contains exactly what you must write to get full marks for the highest-probability topics, including all necessary diagrams, advantages, and limitations required for 7-mark GTU questions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**CHAPTER 1: FOUNDRY TECHNOLOGY**\\n\\n**1. Six Applications of Casting (3 Marks):** Easy Win (Appeared in actual mid-sem). Write these exact 6 points: 1. Automotive engine blocks and cylinder heads. 2. Machine tool beds and frames (due to damping capacity). 3. Turbine blades (aerospace). 4. Railway wheels and tracks. 5. Pump housings and valve bodies. 6. Agricultural machinery components.\\n\\n**2. Pattern Allowances - Theory (7 Marks):** Tier 1. What to write for full marks: • Definition: Intentional dimensional modifications made to a pattern to compensate for metal shrinkage, machining, and casting defects. • 1. Shrinkage Allowance: Metals shrink when cooling from liquid to solid. Pattern is made larger. (Values: CI = 10mm/m, Steel = 20mm/m, Al = 13mm/m). • 2. Machining/Finish Allowance: Extra material added to surfaces that require machining later. (Usually 1.5 to 6 mm). • 3. Draft Allowance: Taper applied to vertical faces of the pattern for easy withdrawal without damaging the mould. (1° to 3° external, 2° to 5° internal). • 4. Shake/Rapping Allowance: When a pattern is shaken to remove it, the mould cavity enlarges. Pattern is made slightly smaller to compensate. (Negative allowance). • 5. Distortion/Camber Allowance: Applied to U or V-shaped castings that tend to warp during cooling. Pattern is bent in the opposite direction. • Diagram Required (Crucial for 7M): Draw a 2D cross-section of a solid block. Show a dotted line outside for \\\"Machining Allowance\\\" and angled vertical sides for \\\"Draft Allowance\\\".\\n\\n**3. Pattern Allowance - Numerical (7 Marks):** Tier 1 (From actual mid-sem). How to score full marks: 1. Read dimensions: Identify L, W, H of the final casting. 2. Add Shrinkage: Add the % or mm/m shrinkage to\n<truncated 7833 bytes>","Description":"\"Cheat sheet content\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\content.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing cheat sheet markdown\"","toolSummary":"\"Write content.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
